  "hindi": "हे पूषन्, इस प्रसव में होता अर्यमा, विधाता, तुम्हारे लिए वषट् करें। ऋत के अनुसार प्रसव करने वाली नारी शिथिल हो जाए, उसके जोड़ प्रसव के लिए खुल जाएँ।",
  "english": "O Pūṣan, in this birthing let Aryaman, the hotṛ priest, the ordainer, make the vaṣaṭ for you. Let the woman, duly delivered, relax; let her joints open apart for the bearing.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Src 'sūtavā ṷ' is sūtavai (Vedic infinitive) + u before a vowel (Devanagari सूत॒वा उ॑); the token ṷ is the particle u. Src 'sūtāv' with ṷ̄ is a transliteration artefact for ū/u. 'ṛta-prajātā' literally 'born/delivered in due order'; sense uncertain. Pūṣan, Aryaman are names of deities; hotṛ is a priest title, here an epithet of Aryaman by apposition. jihatām: form as printed, taken from √hā 'open'.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "001.011.1a",
   "001.011.1b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
